<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνεμό-εις</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμόεις</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>windy,
			airy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἄκριας ἠνεμοέσσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.400
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτὶ Ἴλιον ἠνεμόεσσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.305
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύχας ἠνεμοέσσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.432
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				4.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				781
			</span></i> (lyr.); of Places, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				472
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔρεα ἠ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1129
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of motion,
				<i>rapid, rushing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰγίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					592
				</span></i>
			 codd. (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					953
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγωός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					453
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτευρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					6.444
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμόεν φρόνημα</span>
			<i>high-soaring, airy</i> thought, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				354
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>stirred, waved by the wind</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρινεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.145
				</span></i>
			; <i>filled by the wind</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.92
				</span></i>
			.</div>
